From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julien Etienne <julien.etienne@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 16:31:59 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] serial: core: power a port down when its console is detached

Writing 0 to a port's sysfs "console" attribute unregisters the console,
but the port stays powered for good. uart_configure_port() powered it on
and powers down only non-console ports; uart_console() still matches
after unregister_console(), since it only compares the console index
with the line; tty_port_shutdown() still returns early because
port->console was set once when the port was added; and
uart_resume_port() powers a console port back on after every suspend.
On MediaTek 8250 ports the runtime PM reference that goes with the
power state keeps the UART and its bus clock on, which holds a clock the
SoC's idle states need off.

On detach, clear port->console and power the port off unless it is
open. On re-attach, power it on and set the flag again before
registering. Let a hangup and a resume treat the port as a console only
while its console is registered.
---
 drivers/tty/serial/serial_core.c | 13 +++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/tty/serial/serial_core.c b/drivers/tty/serial/serial_core.c
index 89cebdd27..81f78890b 100644
--- a/drivers/tty/serial/serial_core.c
+++ b/drivers/tty/serial/serial_core.c
@@ -1835,7 +1835,7 @@ static void uart_hangup(struct tty_struct *tty)
 			port->count = 0;
 		tty_port_set_active(port, false);
 		tty_port_tty_set(port, NULL);
-		if (uport && !uart_console(uport))
+		if (uport && !uart_console_registered(uport))
 			uart_change_pm(state, UART_PM_STATE_OFF);
 		wake_up_interruptible(&port->open_wait);
 		wake_up_interruptible(&port->delta_msr_wait);
@@ -2385,7 +2385,7 @@ int uart_resume_port(struct uart_driver *drv, struct uart_port *uport)
 	/*
 	 * Re-enable the console device after suspending.
 	 */
-	if (uart_console(uport)) {
+	if (uart_console_registered(uport)) {
 		/*
 		 * First try to use the console cflag setting.
 		 */
@@ -2976,10 +2976,19 @@ static ssize_t console_store(struct device *dev,
 		ret = unregister_console(uport->cons);
 		if (ret < 0)
 			return ret;
+		/*
+		 * The port is now an ordinary one: let a close shut it down and
+		 * power it off now if nobody has it open, as for any other port.
+		 */
+		port->console = false;
+		if (!tty_port_initialized(port))
+			uart_change_pm(state, UART_PM_STATE_OFF);
 	} else if (!oldconsole && newconsole) {
 		if (!uart_console(uport))
 			return -ENOENT;
 
+		uart_change_pm(state, UART_PM_STATE_ON);
+		port->console = true;
 		uport->console_reinit = 1;
 		register_console(uport->cons);
 	}
